{"id":"mahabharata-7-128","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":128,"title":"अष्टाविंशत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 128 · The night battle begins","summary":{"en":"The Kaurava host surges against the Pandavas in the dark, and Duryodhana, wounded by grief for Jayadratha, vows to fight to the death. He pierces Dhrishtadyumna and Yudhishthira and a great fight follows.","kn":"ಕತ್ತಲಲ್ಲಿ ಕೌರವ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಪಾಂಡವರ ಮೇಲೆ ಉಕ್ಕುತ್ತದೆ; ಜಯದ್ರಥನ ದುಃಖದಿಂದ ನೊಂದ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಸಾಯುವವರೆಗೆ ಹೋರಾಡುವೆನೆಂದು ನಿರ್ಧರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಧೃಷ್ಟದ್ಯುಮ್ನ, ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರರನ್ನು ಚುಚ್ಚುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಮಹಾಯುದ್ಧ ನಡೆಯುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"अँधेरे में कौरव सेना पाण्डवों पर उमड़ती है, और जयद्रथ के शोक से आहत दुर्योधन मृत्यु तक लड़ने का निश्चय करता है। वह धृष्टद्युम्न और युधिष्ठिर को बींधता है और भारी युद्ध होता है।","te":"చీకట్లో కౌరవసేన పాండవులపై ఉప్పొంగుతుంది; జయద్రథుని శోకంతో బాధపడిన దుర్యోధనుడు చచ్చే వరకు పోరాడాలని నిశ్చయిస్తాడు. ధృష్టద్యుమ్నుని, యుధిష్ఠిరుని గుచ్చుతాడు; మహాయుద్ధం జరుగుతుంది.","ta":"இருளில் கௌரவப் படை பாண்டவர் மீது பொங்க, ஜயத்ரதன் குறித்த துயரால் புண்பட்ட துரியோதனன் சாகும்வரை போரிட உறுதிகொள்கிறான். த்ருஷ்டத்யும்னனையும் யுதிஷ்டிரரையும் துளைக்க, பெரும்போர் நடக்கிறது.","ml":"ഇരുട്ടിൽ കൗരവ സേന പാണ്ഡവർക്കെതിരെ ആഞ്ഞടിക്കുന്നു; ജയദ്രഥന്റെ വേർപാടിലെ ദുഃഖത്താൽ മുറിവേറ്റ ദുര്യോധനൻ മരണംവരെ പൊരുതുമെന്ന് പ്രതിജ്ഞയെടുക്കുന്നു. അദ്ദേഹം ധൃഷ്ടദ്യുമ്നനെയും യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെയും അമ്പുകൊണ്ട് തുളയ്ക്കുന്നു; ഘോരമായ യുദ്ധം തുടരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.128; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"घटोत्कचवधपर्व","titleEn":"Ghatotkachavadha Parva (Slaying of Ghatotkacha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तदुदीर्णगजाश्वौघं बलं तव जनाधिप ।\nपाण्डुसेनामभिद्रुत्य योधयामास सर्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, lord of men, your army, with its swollen floods of elephants and horses, rushed on the Pandava army and fought on every side."}},{"n":2,"text":"पाञ्चालाः कुरवश्चैव योधयन्तः परस्परम् ।\nयमराष्ट्राय महते परलोकाय दीक्षिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Panchalas and Kurus fought one another as if consecrated for the great realm of Yama, for the other world."}},{"n":3,"text":"शूराः शूरैः समागम्य शरतोमरशक्तिभिः ।\nविव्यधुः समरे तूर्णं निन्युश्चैव यमक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Heroes met heroes with arrows, spears and lances, quickly pierced one another in battle and sent each other to Yama's abode."}},{"n":4,"text":"रथिनां रथिभिः सार्धं रुधिरस्रावि दारुणम् ।\nप्रावर्तत महद्युद्धं निघ्नतामितरेतरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great, fearful, blood-streaming battle took place between chariot-warriors and chariot-warriors as they killed each other."}},{"n":5,"text":"वारणाश्च महाराज समासाद्य परस्परम् ।\nविषाणैर्दारयामासुः संक्रुद्धाश्च मदोत्कटाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Elephants, O great king, in rut and enraged, met each other and tore at each other with their tusks."}},{"n":6,"text":"हयारोहान्हयारोहाः प्रासशक्तिपरश्वधैः ।\nबिभिदुस्तुमुले युद्धे प्रार्थयन्तो महद्यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horsemen against horsemen in the tumultuous fight, seeking great fame, split each other with lances, spears and axes."}},{"n":7,"text":"पत्तयश्च महाबाहो शतशः शस्त्रपाणयः ।\nअन्योन्यमार्दयन्राजन्नित्ययत्ताः पराक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"And hundreds of foot-soldiers with weapons in hand, mighty-armed one, always eager for valor, crushed each other, O king."}},{"n":8,"text":"गोत्राणां नामधेयानां कुलानां चैव मारिष ।\nश्रवणाद्धि विजानीमः पाञ्चालान्कुरुभिः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"We knew the Panchalas and Kurus fighting only by hearing their clans, names and families."}},{"n":9,"text":"अन्योन्यं समरे योधाः शरशक्तिपरश्वधैः ।\nप्रेषयन्परलोकाय विचरन्तो ह्यभीतवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the battle the warriors, moving fearlessly, sent each other to the other world with arrows, spears and axes."}},{"n":10,"text":"शरैर्दश दिशो राजंस्तेषां मुक्तैः सहस्रशः ।\nन भ्राजन्त यथापूर्वं भास्करेऽस्तं गतेऽपि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"With arrows loosed by them in their thousands, O king, the ten directions did not shine as before, even though the sun had set."}},{"n":11,"text":"तथा प्रयुध्यमानेषु पाण्डवेयेषु निर्भयः ।\nदुर्योधनो महाराज व्यवगाहत तद्बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the Pandavas were fighting so, Duryodhana, fearless, O great king, plunged into their army."}},{"n":12,"text":"सैन्धवस्य वधेनैव भृशं दुःखसमन्वितः ।\nमर्तव्यमिति संचिन्त्य प्राविशत्तु द्विषद्बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Greatly grieved by Saindhava's death, thinking \"I must die,\" he entered the enemy army."}},{"n":13,"text":"नादयन्रथघोषेण कम्पयन्निव मेदिनीम् ।\nअभ्यवर्तत पुत्रस्ते पाण्डवानामनीकिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Making the earth seem to tremble with the noise of his chariot, your son advanced on the Pandava army."}},{"n":14,"text":"स संनिपातस्तुमुलस्तस्य तेषां च भारत ।\nअभवत्सर्वसैन्यानामभावकरणो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That clash, tumultuous, between him and them, O Bharata, brought great destruction to all the armies."}},{"n":15,"text":"मध्यंदिनगतं सूर्यं प्रतपन्तं गभस्तिभिः ।\nतथा तव सुतं मध्ये प्रतपन्तं शरोर्मिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son in their midst, blazing with waves of arrows like the sun at midday scorching with its rays,"}},{"n":16,"text":"न शेकुर्भारतं युद्धे पाण्डवाः समवेक्षितुम् ।\nपलायने कृतोत्साहा निरुत्साहा द्विषज्जये ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Pandavas could not look at the Bharata in battle; eager to flee, they had no heart to conquer."}},{"n":17,"text":"पर्यधावन्त पाञ्चाला वध्यमाना महात्मना ।\nरुक्मपुङ्खैः प्रसन्नाग्रैस्तव पुत्रेण धन्विना ।\nअर्द्यमानाः शरैस्तूर्णं न्यपतन्पाण्डुसैनिकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Panchalas ran about, being killed by that great-souled man, your son, the bowman, with gold-feathered, sharp-pointed arrows, and the Pandava soldiers, tormented by arrows, quickly fell."}},{"n":18,"text":"न तादृशं रणे कर्म कृतवन्तस्तु तावकाः ।\nयादृशं कृतवान्राजा पुत्रस्तव विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your men had not done in battle such a deed as your son the king did, lord of men."}},{"n":19,"text":"पुत्रेण तव सा सेना पाण्डवी मथिता रणे ।\nनलिनी द्विरदेनेव समन्तात्फुल्लपङ्कजा ॥","meaning":{"en":"By your son the Pandava army was churned in battle, as a lotus pond with open lotuses is churned by an elephant."}},{"n":20,"text":"क्षीणतोयानिलार्काभ्यां हतत्विडिव पद्मिनी ।\nबभूव पाण्डवी सेना तव पुत्रस्य तेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava army, by the force of your son, became like a lotus plant robbed of splendor, with its water, air and sun gone."}},{"n":21,"text":"पाण्डुसेनां हतां दृष्ट्वा तव पुत्रेण भारत ।\nभीमसेनपुरोगास्तु पाञ्चालाः समुपाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Pandava army struck by your son, Bharata, the Panchalas led by Bhimasena rushed upon him."}},{"n":22,"text":"स भीमसेनं दशभिर्माद्रीपुत्रौ त्रिभिस्त्रिभिः ।\nविराटद्रुपदौ षड्भिः शतेन च शिखण्डिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He struck Bhimasena with ten arrows, the two sons of Madri with three each, Virata and Drupada with six, and Shikhandi with a hundred,"}},{"n":23,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नं च सप्तत्या धर्मपुत्रं च सप्तभिः ।\nकेकयांश्चैव चेदींश्च बहुभिर्निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna with seventy, the son of Dharma with seven, and the Kekayas and Chedis with many sharp arrows."}},{"n":24,"text":"सात्वतं पञ्चभिर्विद्ध्वा द्रौपदेयांस्त्रिभिस्त्रिभिः ।\nघटोत्कचं च समरे विद्ध्वा सिंह इवानदत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Piercing the Satvata with five and the sons of Draupadi with three each, and wounding Ghatotkacha, he roared like a lion in battle."}},{"n":25,"text":"शतशश्चापरान्योधान्सद्विपाश्वरथान्रणे ।\nशरैरवचकर्तोग्रैः क्रुद्धोऽन्तक इव प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And hundreds of other warriors in battle, with their elephants, horses and chariots, he cut down with fierce arrows, angry like Death among creatures."}},{"n":26,"text":"तस्य तान्निघ्नतः शत्रून्रुक्मपृष्ठं महद्धनुः ।\nभल्लाभ्यां पाण्डवो ज्येष्ठस्त्रिधा चिच्छेद मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he killed those enemies, the eldest Pandava, honorable sir, cut his great gold-backed bow into three with two broad arrows."}},{"n":27,"text":"विव्याध चैनं दशभिः सम्यगस्तैः शितैः शरैः ।\nमर्माणि भित्त्वा ते सर्वे संभग्नाः क्षितिमाविशन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And he pierced him with ten well-shot sharp arrows, which pierced his vitals, broke through and entered the ground."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततः प्रमुदिता योधाः परिवव्रुर्युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nवृत्रहत्यै यथा देवाः परिवव्रुः पुरंदरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the delighted warriors surrounded Yudhishthira as the gods surrounded Indra for the killing of Vritra."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा तव पुत्रस्य मारिष ।\nशरं परमदुर्वारं प्रेषयामास संयुगे ।\nस तेन भृशसंविद्धो निषसाद रथोत्तमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, honorable sir, shot an arrow at your son that was very hard to ward off, and by it, deeply pierced, he sank down on his excellent chariot."}},{"n":30,"text":"ततः पाञ्चालसैन्यानां भृशमासीद्रवो महान् ।\nहतो राजेति राजेन्द्र मुदितानां समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a great uproar rose from the Panchala armies, O king, with the cry \"The king is slain!\" from the delighted warriors on every side."}},{"n":31,"text":"बाणशब्दरवश्चोग्रः शुश्रुवे तत्र मारिष ।\nअथ द्रोणो द्रुतं तत्र प्रत्यदृश्यत संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"A terrible noise of arrows was heard there, honorable sir, and then Drona was suddenly seen there in the battle."}},{"n":32,"text":"हृष्टो दुर्योधनश्चापि दृढमादाय कार्मुकम् ।\nतिष्ठ तिष्ठेति राजानं ब्रुवन्पाण्डवमभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Delighted, Duryodhana too took a strong bow and went against the Pandava king, saying \"Stand! Stand!\""}},{"n":33,"text":"प्रत्युद्ययुस्तं त्वरिताः पाञ्चाला राजगृद्धिनः ।\nतान्द्रोणः प्रतिजग्राह परीप्सन्कुरुसत्तमम् ।\nचण्डवातोद्धतान्मेघान्निघ्नन्रश्मिमुचो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Panchalas, eager for the king, hurried to meet him, but Drona received them, wishing to protect the best of the Kurus, like the sun's rays dispersing clouds driven by a fierce wind."}},{"n":34,"text":"ततो राजन्महानासीत्संग्रामो भूरिवर्धनः ।\nतावकानां परेषां च समेतानां युयुत्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, a great and growing battle took place between your men and the enemy, who had met wishing to fight."}}]}]}